    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0753" n="665" xml:id="pg665"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 862.5018/7</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the American Embassy in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-15">15 December,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Mr. Hoover has asked me
                    to send you herewith a dossier of memoranda and correspondence in regard to the
                    proposed plan for the Relief of Europe.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d547-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>As Mr. Hoover is to submit these documents to the President this evening, he is
                    anxious that they should be laid before you as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh Gibson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d547-f1" n="31" xml:id="d547-f1-content">
                <p>Dossier included the letter of Dec. 1, 1918, from Colonel House to Mr. Balfour;
                    the memorandum of the conference held in London, Dec. 10; the statement
                    submitted to the conference by Messrs. Hoover and Davis, Dec. 10; the report of
                    the committee appointed by the Allied Premiers, dated Dec. 12; and the undated
                    memorandum by Messrs. Hoover, Davis, and Cotton; <ref target="#pg646">pp.
                        646</ref>, <ref target="#pg649">649</ref>, <ref target="#pg651">651</ref>,
                        <ref target="#pg654">654</ref>, and <ref target="#pg658">658</ref>,
                    respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
